    faq: [['Are the mappings official?', 'There is no single official table across the four frameworks. The map is the author’s judgement, checked against an ENS ↔ ISO/IEC 27001 SoA template and ENISA technical guidance. Review it with your auditor.'], ['Why does a requirement depend on several controls?', 'Frameworks group things differently: ENS op.exp.7 asks for a complete incident process, which Rosetta splits into plan, classification, response, lessons and reporting.'], ['Does importing my ENS SoA mark everything?', 'Controls mapped to the ENS inherit state, owners and evidence. Whatever the ENS does not ask for stays pending.'], ['Is NIS2 already mandatory in Spain?', 'The directive is in force, but as of September 2026 the Spanish transposition law is still going through parliament. Rosetta applies the directive.'], ['Where is my data stored?', 'Only in this browser. Use Settings → Backup to take your projects elsewhere.']],
